# Governance documents retired by PR #278. /workplace-policy and
# /whistleblower-policy were live, linked-to pages (member emails, inductions)
# replaced by the one "How We Work Together" framework — so they redirect to it
# rather than 404. Workers static assets do NOT normalise trailing slashes, so
# each path needs both forms (the site itself serves the slashed one). Static
# rules sit above the :id placeholder rules below, which is the order Cloudflare
# evaluates most cheaply.
/workplace-policy       /how-we-work-together  301
/workplace-policy/      /how-we-work-together  301
/whistleblower-policy   /how-we-work-together  301
/whistleblower-policy/  /how-we-work-together  301

# Old Qomon-hosted form/page URLs. The pre-rebuild site 301'd to these, and
# browsers replay those cached permanent redirects without contacting the
# server — so the stale destinations must keep landing somewhere useful.
/forms/:id/join-the-australian-democrats      /join     301
/forms/:id/donate-to-the-australian-democrats /donate   301
/pages/:id/contact-us                         /contact  301
